{"uid":"dd75cec035904dd3","name":"test_a_tampered_record_surfaces_the_obligation_again","fullName":"tests.test_confirmed_petition_not_resurfaced#test_a_tampered_record_surfaces_the_obligation_again","historyId":"7af07d35cd780250782dc71faf9e4f10","time":{"start":1791916024187,"stop":1791916024195,"duration":8},"description":"#209 §5 widened this node from the CONFIRMED half to both verdicts:\n    the record now carries a CONFIRMED entry for the first obligation AND a\n    REFUTED entry for the second, so the tamper posture is pinned for the\n    SETTLED reader (`settled_obligations`) as well as the exemption reader\n    (`confirmed_obligations`). Both must read empty and both petitions must\n    render again. Nothing is relaxed -- every assertion the CONFIRMED-only\n    version made is still made verbatim; the REFUTED entry and the\n    `settled_obligations` assertion are additions. The direction matters\n    for the new reader in a way it did not for the old one: an unreadable\n    record must not be allowed to look like a settlement, or a hand-edit\n    could keep a genuinely open obligation out of review's prompt\n    altogether.","descriptionHtml":"<p>#209 §5 widened this node from the CONFIRMED half to both verdicts:<br />\nthe record now carries a CONFIRMED entry for the first obligation AND a<br />\nREFUTED entry for the second, so the tamper posture is pinned for the<br />\nSETTLED reader (<code>settled_obligations</code>) as well as the exemption reader<br />\n(<code>confirmed_obligations</code>). Both must read empty and both petitions must<br />\nrender again. Nothing is relaxed -- every assertion the CONFIRMED-only<br />\nversion made is still made verbatim; the REFUTED entry and the<br />\n<code>settled_obligations</code> assertion are additions. The direction matters<br />\nfor the new reader in a way it did not for the old one: an unreadable<br />\nrecord must not be allowed to look like a settlement, or a hand-edit<br />\ncould keep a genuinely open o